            <ArticleTitle>Ticlopidine-carbamazepine interaction in a coronary stent patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>853-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Neurological symptoms occurred in association with increased carbamazepine levels because of a probable drug interaction between ticlopidine and carbamazepine in an epileptic patient undergoing coronary stenting. Physicians should be aware of this possible drug interaction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
